{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_i5bamtyoto7ojqlhougelc6u3nglt5qnuvmdf3kyiy3xfbwzhtwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte across all tested surfaces.\n\n## Results\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (in `translation/`):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 78 `libcjson.so` symbols + `driver` are exported by the Rust `.so`; **0 missing**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols. Extras: `cJSON_Duplicate_rec` (non-`static` in C, only hidden by `-fvisibility=hidden`) and `driver`.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 121 rejection rows derived from every `return NULL`/`return false`/`goto fail`/range check/limit constant in `cJSON.c`, each mapped to a passing test (row 32 documented as unreachable in-process).\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 76 valid-path configuration rows (hooks variants, format flags, `require_null_terminated`, `buffer_length`, prebuffer sizes, all 8 types × modifier bits, etc.), all checked off.\n\n**Tests** — 11 files, 93 tests, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and comparing returns, item fields, structural fingerprints, `prev`/`next` link bookkeeping, printed bytes, and error-pointer offsets. `driver` stdout is captured via `dup2` and compared byte-for-byte. Passes in debug and release; the crate has no `[features]` and no `cfg(feature)` in `src/`.\n\n## Two harness bugs I found and fixed\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds the cdylib** — the harness was silently testing a stale `.so`. It now rebuilds the lib into `target/so/` at test start and asserts the `.so` is newer than every source file. Before this fix, injected bugs went undetected.\n2. **Global-state races** — `global_error`/`global_hooks` are per-library process globals; parallel tests clobbered them. Tests that observe them now take a shared mutex.\n\n## Mutation-adequacy check\nI injected 40 single-token bugs into `src/cjson.rs` one at a time; 36 were caught. That exposed three real coverage gaps, now closed with new tests:\n- the `\\uXXXX` decoder (`utf16_literal_to_utf8`) was untested → added exhaustive sweeps of all 65 536 BMP escapes, all surrogate halves, the supplementary plane, and 33 malformed escape forms;\n- exact-size boundaries → BOM at every `buffer_length` (`skip_utf8_bom` needs 5 readable bytes) and `PrintPreallocated`/`PrintBuffered` at every buffer length;\n- prefix-sensitive comparisons → randomized mixed-case keys/probes and strings sharing prefixes for `case_insensitive_strcmp` and `cJSON_Compare`.\n\nThe 4 remaining survivors are provably equivalent mutants (documented in `CONFIGS.md`), e.g. `parse_number`'s `>= INT_MAX` vs `>` yields the same `valueint` at exactly `2147483647.0`.\n\nNo divergences remain: `src/` is byte-identical to its pre-testing state (verified against 7 independent backups) — every fix was in the tests, never in the C.\n\nOne note for your judgement: two error-table expectations I first wrote were wrong about the C, and I corrected the table to match the C rather than the reverse — a `cJSON_String` item with `valuestring == NULL` prints `\"\"` (only `cJSON_Raw` fails), and `cJSON_Duplicate` of such an item succeeds with `valuestring == NULL`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":320090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":786,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"367dd387-5e5c-4b28-a2db-180d222aa07c","uuid":"7b00ca66-259a-46c5-82a3-30700ba5ae1a","timestamp":"2026-09-05T07:04:48.212Z"}
